    "tag_name": "optima-core-v1.6.0.1",
    "draft": false,
    "prerelease": false,
    "body": "## 1.6.0.1 (2026-10-28)\n\n- Editable pages (upstream 1.6.0 feature, Optima revision 1). A designed page's words and photos are edited on the page in the block editor; the layout, icons and theme parts stay locked with WordPress's content-only lock. Themes opt in with `add_theme_support( 'optima-editable-pages', array( 'content_dir' => ..., 'editor_css' => array( ... ) ) )` and call `optima_core_render_editable()` where the page body goes. Five blocks (`optima/box`, `optima/text`, `optima/image`, `optima/frozen`, `optima/part`), a Page photos panel, theme parts through the `optima_core_editable_part` filter, import that fills empty pages and refreshes untouched ones but never overwrites an edited page, and FAQ structured data rebuilt from the visible questions (`optima_schema_graph`, or `optima_core_editable_faq()` for themes that print their own schema).\n- Administrators can rearrange a page with WordPress's \"Edit pattern\" button; clients and editors get the lock on the whole editor and no unlock button.\n- Build tool for client repos: `tools/editable-pages/build_blocks.py` (not shipped in the plugin).\n- Nothing changes for themes that do not opt in.",
    "assets": [
      {
        "name": "optima-core.zip",
        "browser_download_url": "https://github.com/optimadigitalmedia/Optima-Plugins/releases/download/optima-core-v1.6.0.1/optima-core.zip"
